cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Observatoire Laudisi: a continuous multimodal observatory of
  French rolling-news television
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it using the metadata
  in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: de Boisvilliers
    given-names: Yann
    email: yann.deboisvilliers@psl.eu
    affiliation: Université Paris-Dauphine–PSL / EHESS
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
abstract: >-
  Observatoire Laudisi is a research instrument that has
  captured, transcribed and analysed French rolling-news
  television continuously since March 2026: four national
  channels (BFMTV, CNews, franceinfo, LCI) and seventeen
  regional ones (10 BFM local stations, 7 France 3 stations).
  Audio and keyframes are recorded 24/7 and aligned on a
  single timeline — spoken word, speaker identity and
  on-screen banners — supporting the study of agenda
  convergence between channels, framing divergence at
  constant topic, and the circadian structure of continuous
  news programming.
keywords:
  - computational social science
  - media sociology
  - television news
  - agenda setting
  - multimodal corpora
  - speech-to-text
  - speaker diarization
